 of the buffer (or marked region) will be piped to the command.  If
 you just need another blank buffer, do not enter any command.

 You can also pick one of four tools, or cut a large piece of the
 buffer, or put the editor to sleep.

 The following function keys are available in Execute Command mode:

^G     (F1)      Display this help text
^C               Cancel the current function

M-F              Toggle the use of a new buffer
M-\              Pipe the current buffer (or marked region) to the
		   command

^S     (^T)      Invoke the spell checker, if available
^Y               Invoke the linter, if available

^J               Justify the entire file
^O               Invoke a program to format/arrange/manipulate the
		   buffer

^V               Cut from the cursor position to the end of the file

^Z               Suspend the editor (return to the shell)
